    {
      "id": "43b5b152-bbf9-4ee8-bf2d-e06c3d15c57b",
      "name": "Validate Enquiry Contact",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        1312,
        352
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "return $input.all().map((i,index)=>{const j=i.json;const email=String(j.email||'').trim();if(!/^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/.test(email))throw Error('A valid contact email is required; no messages sent');return {json:{...j,email},pairedItem:{item:index}};});"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "81f33c49-5ab5-4446-849b-9cd79cf0c825",
      "name": "Start here",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 264,
        "content": "## Start here\n\nTurn a sponsorship form submission into a logged sales enquiry and an appropriate follow-up. The model suggests a fit tier and an opening paragraph; the sales team owns the offer and final proposal.\n\nHigh-fit leads receive a proposal-style reply and a Telegram alert. Medium-fit leads receive an introductory reply. Low-fit leads are logged without an automatic email."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "5962e106-f4bc-448f-858a-66d2d32e407e",
      "name": "Connect and configure",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        352
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 460,
        "content": "## Connect and configure\n\n1. Select Header Auth on the sponsorship-inquiry webhook and send requests through a trusted server.\n2. POST companyName, contactName, email, budgetRange, industry and eventInterest. A valid email is required.\n3. Connect OpenAI and review the sample sponsorship packages in the qualification prompt. Replace them with your real offer.\n4. Choose the spreadsheet and Sponsorship Leads tab. Create columns matching Shape Output: companyName, contactName, email, budgetRange, industry, eventInterest, fitTier, matchedSponsorshipLevel, proposalOpening, reasoning and loggedAt.\n5. Connect Gmail and Telegram; set the sales chat. Review both email messages before enabling the webhook."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c93465bd-f665-424a-8d76-703c0ef2b65f",
      "name": "Before switching on",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        16,
        896
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 372,
        "content": "## Before switching on\n\nUse contact addresses and a sales chat you control. Test high, medium and low fit, an empty email and an invalid model response. Confirm the complete sheet row and the correct branch.\n\nThis version sends replies automatically; add a human approval step if your process requires draft review. It does not include a sales deck, schedule a call or promise a response time.\n\nService failures stop the run. Before replaying a failed run, check whether a row or email was already created. No exactly-once delivery is claimed."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "6f1fc314-1911-4397-bf55-9159c40f5423",
      "name": "1. Accept and validate the enquiry",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        640,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1040,
        "height": 590,
        "content": "## 1. Accept and validate the enquiry\n\nNormalization reads the contact, company, budget and event-interest fields and records the submission time. Validate Enquiry Contact rejects a missing or malformed email before the model or email steps run.\n\nKeep the form's field names aligned with Normalize Input. Protect the webhook secret on your server."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "6d8ac780-f87d-4d42-a526-b24c43fa3b6a",
      "name": "2. Suggest fit using your sponsorship offer",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1760,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 1040,
        "height": 820,
        "content": "## 2. Suggest fit using your sponsorship offer\n\nThe prompt contains the sample package levels and qualification instructions. Edit those before using this with prospects. The model returns high, medium or low fit, a suggested package, an opening paragraph and its reasoning.\n\nThe parser defines the required structure. Shape Output rejects incomplete results and combines valid output with the original contact record."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "58baa800-bea8-4f41-b903-ac99425ccd0c",
      "name": "3. Log the result before choosing a reply",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2880,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1040,
        "height": 590,
        "content": "## 3. Log the result before choosing a reply\n\nSheets appends the enquiry and qualification fields. The switch reads fitTier from Shape Output, rather than relying on the spreadsheet response to contain the original lead.\n\nHigh and medium outputs have email paths. Low fit intentionally ends after logging. Unexpected tiers fail validation earlier; they must not silently receive a standard reply."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "2d348018-f019-4a6b-9882-6a335a90eeb3",
      "name": "4. Send the configured follow-up",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        4000,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 1040,
        "height": 590,
        "content": "## 4. Send the configured follow-up\n\nThe high-fit email includes the generated opening paragraph, then alerts the sales lead in Telegram. The medium-fit email asks for the event and desired outcomes.\n\nBoth use plain text and the retained contact record. Neither claims an attachment is included or that a call is booked. Add your real information-pack link and approved sales wording if needed."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
